WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.520 line:87%
I believe this programme
is probably one of the best things

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.280 line:94%
that has happened to me in my life.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.600 line:87%
You make a lot of new friends.
You gain confidence.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.600 line:94%
You experience new cultures.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.480 line:94%
My expectations and hopes

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.240 line:87%
included meeting new people
and improving my English.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.200 line:87%
I already knew some English,
but I wanted to improve.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:29.720 line:87%
I chose this programme
because the challenge for me

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.200 line:87%
was to be away from home
and my family

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.160 line:94%
for a period of time.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.600 line:87%
We're from five different cultures
and speak five different languages,

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:42.000 line:94%
but this isn't a negative thing.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:45.120 line:87%
It's positive
because it's an opportunity for learning.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:54.760 line:87%
The aim of the project
is to develop these soft skills -

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:58.120 line:94%
confidence in yourself and in others,

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.640 line:87%
the ability to interact
with different cultures

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.440 line:87%
and the self-confidence
to take on challenges

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:07.320 line:87%
through games and
especially street arts,

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.160 line:87%
such as clownery,
juggling and acrobatics.

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:19.440 line:87%
In clownery you need to come out
of your comfort zone to an extent.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:24.320 line:87%
You must dare to be ridiculous,
dare to fail,

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:27.680 line:87%
fail also in a funny way,
to laugh at yourself, laugh at others.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:32.440 line:94%
I learnt how to be myself with others

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:35.760 line:87%
and not have to pretend
to be somebody else.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.480 line:87%
And I learnt how to be open with other
people, which is the main thing.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:44.040 line:94%
I think we're all essentially the same.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:48.400 line:87%
We're different
in terms of our customs and traditions,

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:51.600 line:94%
but as people we're not different at all.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.120 line:87%
You learn a lot more
about your European neighbours

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.640 line:87%
and you feel more part
of the European community.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.640 line:87%
My greatest moment
will have to be last night on the stage

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.240 line:94%
when we all came together.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.440 line:94%
It was like a climax of this exchange.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.040 line:87%
There was a great energy
behind the stage.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:11.800 line:87%
All the hard work we put in
and all the friends we made.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:14.080 line:94%
We really showed that on the stage.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.720 line:94%
We've seen a lot of young people

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.720 line:94%
who through the Erasmus and Youth in

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.080 line:87%
Action exchange and
training programmes

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:26.000 line:87%
have changed and grown
and have followed very different paths.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.280 line:87%
Some didn't want to go to university,
but now have enrolled,

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:33.280 line:94%
some have gone on an EVS year,

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.960 line:87%
people who didn't know anything
about Erasmus before

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:39.760 line:94%
or couldn't speak English.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.520 line:87%
It's only because they've done
something different

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.640 line:87%
that they have decided
to take on these challenges.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:47.560 line:94%
Erasmus+!

